# PayKit — example environment variables
#
# Copy this file to `.env` and fill in real values for the providers you use.
# All variables are OPTIONAL: PayKit works out of the box with the in-memory
# MockProvider and requires no credentials. Provide these only when wiring up a
# real provider (Stripe) or verifying real webhooks.
#
# ⚠️  NEVER commit your real `.env` file or any live secret keys. `.env` is
#     already listed in .gitignore. Use test keys (sk_test_..., whsec_...) for
#     development.

# ─── Stripe ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Stripe secret API key. Used by StripeProvider to create/refund payments.
# Test keys start with sk_test_, live keys with sk_live_.
STRIPE_SECRET_KEY=sk_test_your_stripe_secret_key_here

# Stripe webhook signing secret. Used by WebhookEngine to verify the
# `stripe-signature` header (HMAC-SHA256). Found in the Stripe Dashboard under
# Developers → Webhooks. Starts with whsec_.
STRIPE_WEBHOOK_SECRET=whsec_your_stripe_webhook_signing_secret_here

# ─── Frontend playground (optional) ───────────────────────────────────────────
# Base URL of an OPTIONAL PayKit backend for the Next.js playground.
#
# The playground (frontend/) runs the REAL paykit SDK entirely in the browser,
# so this is NOT required — leave it unset to run in default "In-browser SDK"
# (demo) mode. If you stand up a backend that exposes the same primitives over
# HTTP (e.g. a POST /fraud/check endpoint and a GET /health probe), set this and
# the playground will try the live backend first, then fall back to the
# in-browser SDK on any error. Must be prefixed NEXT_PUBLIC_ to be readable in
# the browser bundle.
# NEXT_PUBLIC_API_URL=http://localhost:8000
